Patch 0088: the function table is a static const {address, function} array plus don_game_module(), not a static constructor.
What: the emitter (function_table_emitter.cpp) writes `static const DonFunctionEntry g_donFunctionEntries[]` and
`const DonGameModule &don_game_module()` instead of GeneratedFunctionTableInitializer. ps2_runtime.h declares DonFunctionEntry,
DonGameModule and don_game_module(). The PS2Runtime constructor copies the array into the writable g_ps2RecompiledFunctionTable
(unchanged name and size, still defined by the generated file); replaceFunction/overrides keep writing there. The runner fallback
and the unit-test table return an empty module. The constructor copies through ps2FillRecompiledFunctionTable(), which prints
"[don] function table entry N has address 0x... outside [...)" and aborts for an address outside the table or not word-aligned.
Tests: code_generator_tests and ps2_recompiler_tests expectations follow the new text. The fill has three cases: the in-range fill (resets the table at its end), and two aborts checked in a forked child (SIGABRT) for an address outside the table and for an unaligned address; POSIX only, skipped on Windows.
Verified: ps2x_tests with this patch: 431 pass, 10 fail (pre-existing, the same cases as at the pinned base). With the check removed from the fill, the two abort cases fail (12 fail).
Route: game regenerated and built; fight_practice:
all 32 `[don] state blank` lines equal work/baseline/fight_practice.state (screenshot md5s differ in the sandbox even unpatched).
Origin: original to this project.
